"comparison": "Both Citigroup (C) and Bank of America (BAC) reported a decrease in their total allowance for credit losses (ACL/ACLL) for the fiscal year 2024. However, the scale and drivers differed significantly. Citigroup's corporate ACLL decreased by approximately $158 million (from $2,714 million to $2,556 million), driven primarily by releases for specific risks in vulnerable industries and transfer risks outside the U.S. In contrast, Bank of America's total ACL decreased by $215 million to $14.3 billion, driven by decreases in commercial and consumer real estate portfolios, partially offset by increases in consumer credit card and small business loans.",
